From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] waveydude: fresh render targets leave early under memory pressure; a pipeline worker retries once after out of memory

Two of the three changes of waveydude/Eglantine-PS5- (branch ocarina-t85-town, commit d7b5103bd),
ported onto this tree; the third, his driver patch for the scratch rings, is in the driver series as
lead-mesh-26. All are off unless set.

- EDEN_NX2_RT_EVICT_PRESSURE=1 (exact 1; his inner patch 0913, from PS5_Lichii 0227 by mihawk-99,
  Fritchii#34 / Lichii#1023 by Ghostwolf13). A render target of a Switch 2 title that the GPU has
  never written starts undefined instead of loading the guest memory under it, and is queued.
  While the texture cache is over its expected size, a queued target not used for
  EDEN_NX2_RT_EVICT_AGE_FRAMES frames (1 to 3600, 60 when unset or unreadable) is deleted without
  a download. One that is bound, decoding or waiting for a download is checked again, four times
  at most, then counts as lasting. Boot-fixed: the queue is state. His tree takes the age in the
  switch itself (=120); here that form logs one line saying how to write it.
  On top of his logic, from our review: a target whose contents the guest reads back is never
  dropped (relocation_guard_noted, forced_flushed, dma_downloaded: the cold sweep's own rule), at
  most 16 deletions a frame as the cold sweep, and the hitch trace names the reason "rt-evict".
  The image flag is bit 25 (24 is GuestBytes here).
- EDEN_NX2_GRAPHICS_PIPELINE_OOM_RETRY=1 (exact 1; his inner patch 0912). A graphics pipeline
  built on a worker that fails with out of host or device memory asks the front end for 16 MiB
  back (eden_radv_out_of_memory, the same call the driver's own retry makes), sleeps 16 ms and
  tries once more; a second failure takes the existing path (0532: the pipeline is left out). A
  live switch (common/live_switch.h): each creation reads it once and keeps nothing.
  One log line per 10 s at most: "... recovered a pipeline" or "... retry failed".

What the console has to show for the first: a target that starts undefined shows garbage if a game
draws onto guest-prepared memory without clearing it, and one dropped after its idle time and read
later would be stale or black (a pause or map backdrop). Look for "RT evict: N unused fresh render
targets deleted early so far".

Drafted with an AI tool and reviewed (anchors of prepare-vulkan-port.py counted per file:
unchanged); not left in: his inner 0488, which our 0516 already covers.

